WEBVTT

00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:03.172
PostgreSQL provides several case functions.

00:00:03.172 --> 00:00:05.857
UPPER makes all letters uppercase.

00:00:05.857 --> 00:00:12.437
LOWER makes all letters lowercase and is commonly useful for normalization before comparison.

00:00:12.437 --> 00:00:16.687
INITCAP capitalizes words for display.

00:00:16.687 --> 00:00:22.962
Be careful with names because real capitalization can be more complex than a simple function.

00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:29.882
A cleaning rule should fit the domain rather than assuming one display convention is universally correct.

00:00:29.882 --> 00:00:34.087
Text cleaning should separate normalization from interpretation.

00:00:34.087 --> 00:00:39.947
Trimming spaces or standardizing case is usually safe when the rule is documented;

00:00:39.947 --> 00:00:45.932
correcting a person's name or guessing an email address is a much stronger intervention.

00:00:45.932 --> 00:00:49.398
Preserve the original value when auditability matters.
